Package: popgridR
Title: Mosaic Cartograms from Arbitrary Boundaries and Weights
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Georgios", "Karamanis", , "georgios.karamanis@me.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Generate mosaic (block) cartograms: a set of regions is
    deformed so that area is proportional to a numeric weight, then
    rasterised into equal-area square cells, with each region receiving a
    cell count fixed by largest-remainder (Hamilton) allocation. Works
    with any 'sf' polygon input and any numeric weight (population,
    trips, GDP, ...). Deformation can use 'cartogramR' (Dougenik et al.
    1985 <doi:10.1111/j.0033-0124.1985.00075.x>; Gastner and Newman 2004
    <doi:10.1073/pnas.0400280101>) or a built-in dependency-free damped
    Dougenik implementation. Post-processing enforces exact per-region
    cell counts, repairs adjacency against true geography, and fills
    interior gaps. R port and generalisation of the 'popgrid' 'Python'
    package.
